From 3a05455291b8fdb079a18797c2a21a7b70fd97d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dsh-local <dsh-local@localhost>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:49:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add per-device browser access tokens and a Settings page to
 manage them

Browser authentication had one process-scoped launch token shared by every
browser, so an operator could not issue a login link for one device, see which
devices were signed in, or sign one out without restarting the process.

Connection now owns a durable access directory at
client-connection/browser-access holding named login tokens and the devices
they authorized. A cookie minted from a stored token names its device, so a
revocation refuses that device's next request. The process launch token stays
outside the directory as the recovery entry, and version-1 cookies keep
authenticating as unmanaged sessions, so no existing browser is signed out by
the upgrade.

The settings surface is one new client package over a generated browserAccess
Remote namespace.
